  <!-- SECTION 1 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">v1.0 — Initial Launch</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      The foundational release of JuliaOS introduced the core architecture and established the system’s 
      identity as a cognitive operating system. This version included:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• Gameboard Interface:</strong> The primary visualization layer.<br>
      <strong>• Analytical Craft Engine:</strong> The structured analysis mechanic.<br>
      <strong>• Inquiry Pattern:</strong> The disciplined questioning framework.<br>
      <strong>• Human‑System Interface:</strong> The module for interpreting human behavior.<br>
      <strong>• Continuity Suite:</strong> The resilience and stability layer.<br>
      <strong>• Rulebook:</strong> The governing document for system mechanics and philosophy.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 2 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">v1.1 — Inquiry Pattern Enhancements</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      This update refined the Inquiry Pattern by expanding the question taxonomy and improving the 
      sequencing logic. Enhancements included:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• New boundary question types</strong> for clarifying scope.<br>
      <strong>• Improved contradiction detection</strong> for narrative vs. reality gaps.<br>
      <strong>• Integration hooks</strong> for smoother interaction with the Gameboard Interface.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 3 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">v1.2 — Human‑System Interface Refinements</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      This release deepened the system’s ability to interpret human behavior and emotional signals. 
      Updates included:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• Expanded energy state categories</strong> for more accurate interpretation.<br>
      <strong>• Enhanced communication‑pattern mapping</strong> for cross‑team analysis.<br>
      <strong>• New emotional signal indicators</strong> integrated into the Analytical Craft Engine.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 4 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">v1.3 — Continuity Suite Integration</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      This update strengthened the resilience layer of JuliaOS by integrating the Continuity Suite more 
      deeply into the system’s core mechanics. Improvements included:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• Scenario modeling templates</strong> for stress‑testing assumptions.<br>
      <strong>• Stability mapping enhancements</strong> for identifying fragile components.<br>
      <strong>• Risk interpretation pathways</strong> connected to the Gameboard Interface.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 5 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">v1.4 — Expansion Framework Launch</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      This release introduced the modular expansion system, allowing JuliaOS to grow without disrupting 
      the core architecture. Additions included:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• Expansion compatibility model</strong> for seamless integration.<br>
      <strong>• New mechanics expansion slots</strong> for future modules.<br>
      <strong>• The Scenario Deck</strong> as the first official expansion pack.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 6 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">v1.5 — Visual & Structural Refinements</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      This update aligned all JuliaOS pages to the Rulebook layout, improving readability, consistency, 
      and user experience. Enhancements included:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• Unified typography system</strong> across all modules.<br>
      <strong>• Single‑column layout</strong> for clarity and calm navigation.<br>
      <strong>• Removal of legacy card/grid components</strong> from OS pages.<br>
      <strong>• Deloitte‑green section titles</strong> for brand consistency.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- SECTION 7 -->
  <section class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Future Roadmap</h2>
    <p class="section-body">
      JuliaOS is designed to evolve. Future releases may include:
    </p>
    <p class="section-body">
      <strong>• Alignment Engine 2.0</strong> with enhanced conflict‑resolution mechanics.<br>
      <strong>• Expanded Human‑System models</strong> for deeper behavioral insight.<br>
      <strong>• New visualization modes</strong> for the Gameboard Interface.<br>
      <strong>• Additional continuity stress packs</strong> for advanced scenario testing.<br>
      <strong>• Entirely new worlds</strong> added through major expansions.
    </p>
  </section>

